          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt9comzw1lwkjtum",
          "message": {
            "text": "Global :focus-visible ring lives here so every focusable control inherits one visible keyboard-focus indicator — Glassbox is keyboard-driven (j/k nav, Cmd+Enter), so this is load-bearing, not cosmetic.\n\nTwo non-obvious specificity details make it actually show:\n\n- Components that previously killed the outline with a bare &:focus { outline: none } had to change, because :focus-visible also matches on keyboard focus, and a class-level :focus rule (higher specificity) would win and re-hide the ring. They now scope the suppression to &:focus:not(:focus-visible) (see the settings-select rule here (0)) — mouse focus stays clean, keyboard focus keeps the ring.\n- .segment and .settings-tab use an inset ring (outline-offset: -2px) because their container has overflow: hidden; a positive offset would be clipped at the group edge.\n\nGuarded by a conventions test that fails if any SCSS reintroduces &:focus { outline: none } without the :not(:focus-visible) companion.\n",
            "markdown": "Global `:focus-visible` ring lives here so every focusable control inherits one visible keyboard-focus indicator — Glassbox is keyboard-driven (j/k nav, Cmd+Enter), so this is load-bearing, not cosmetic.\n\nTwo non-obvious specificity details make it actually show:\n\n- Components that previously killed the outline with a bare `&:focus { outline: none }` had to change, because `:focus-visible` *also* matches on keyboard focus, and a class-level `:focus` rule (higher specificity) would win and re-hide the ring. They now scope the suppression to `&:focus:not(:focus-visible)` (see the settings-select rule [here](0)) — mouse focus stays clean, keyboard focus keeps the ring.\n- `.segment` and `.settings-tab` use an inset ring (`outline-offset: -2px`) because their container has `overflow: hidden`; a positive offset would be clipped at the group edge.\n\nGuarded by a conventions test that fails if any SCSS reintroduces `&:focus { outline: none }` without the `:not(:focus-visible)` companion.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/styles/_base.scss"
                },
